# --- s062 Book I d.24 q. un. (pp. 98–99; B81L–B82L approx.)
n("n1128","s062-01","vtrum in diuinis sit proprie numerus","la","source","Scotus, *Ord.* I d. 24 q. un. (*Utrum in divinis sit numerus*; Wadding text checked locally). Gorris’s four articles (real/rational being; absolute/relative form; nine conclusions; reply) are not Scotus’s order and seem to be his own digest or a later Scotist’s (Meyronnes possible).","to-verify")
n("n1129","s062-01","tu deus solus es","la","intertext","Ps 85:10 (Vulg. *tu es Deus solus*); cf. 4 Kgs 19:15 and Is 37:16. The argument from *solitudo* is in Lombard, *Sent.* I d. 24 and Scotus.","probable")
n("n1130","s062-03","dicit sanctus doctor quod est ens rationis","la","source","Aquinas: number in God as something of reason. Probable loci: *In I Sent.* d. 24 q. 1 a. 3; *ST* I q. 30 a. 3. Not yet checked.","to-verify")
n("n1131","s062-03","nam non est circumscripto intellectu. 4. phisicorum","la","source","Aristotle, *Phys.* IV 14, 223a21–29: if there were no soul there would be no number (and no time), since only soul or intellect can number. *anima est numerans* below refers to the same passage.","certain")
n("n1132","s062-03","Scotum et sequaces eius","la","textual","B omits *eius*. B checked.","certain")
n("n1133","s062-05","respectus intrinsecus adueniens. quia ponitur positis extremis","la","doctrinal","Scotist terminology: a relation *intrinsecus adveniens* arises necessarily once its extremes are posited (likeness, equality, number), unlike a relation *extrinsecus adveniens*. B garbles this: *respectus intransitus adueniens quia predicatur presentis extremis*. A is correct. B checked.","certain")
n("n1134","s062-05","vt videbitur in secundo","la","commentary","Cross-reference to Book II (Lombard, *Sent.* II d. 9, on the orders of angels).","probable")
n("n1135","s062-05","et vnitas priuatiua","la","textual","B: *cum numerus sit forma positiua et positiuum non constituitur pro parua tantum et ideo numerus non constituitur ex vnitatibus .ix. metha.* B omits *et vnitas priuatiua*, corrupts *per priuatiuum* into *pro parua tantum*, and has *non constituitur ex vnitatibus* where A has *constituitur vno*. B checked.","certain")
n("n1136","s062-05","constituitur vno. 9. metha.","la","source","Aristotle, *Metaph.* X 1 (unity as the measure and principle of number), here numbered *9*. The medieval Latin numbering of the books varied. The numbering has not been checked.","to-verify")
n("n1137","s062-05","nam sex est semel sex","la","source","Aristotle, *Metaph.* V 14, 1020b7–8: six is not twice three but once six. B: *Nam sex vel semel sexies*. B checked.","certain")
n("n1138","s062-05","ex vnitatibus aggregata","la","intertext","Cf. Euclid, *Elem.* VII def. 2, and Boethius, *Inst. arith.* I 3 (*numerus est unitatum collectio*); Aristotle, *Metaph.* X 1, 1053a30 (number as a plurality of units). B: *aggrauata*, an error. B checked.","probable")
n("n1139","s062-06","primo celi","la","source","Aristotle, *De caelo* I 1, 268a10–20: the triad is the number of the whole.","certain")
n("n1140","s062-06","Item tres sunt qui testimonium dant in celo","la","intertext","1 Jn 5:7 (the *Comma Johanneum* of the Vulgate).","certain")
n("n1141","s062-07","ponit solitudinem scriptura","la","textual","B: *similitudinem*, an error for *solitudinem*. B checked.","certain")
n("n1142","s062-04","Quantum ad secundum articulum","la","textual","Signature at the foot of p. 99 printed *g.z* (= g.2). Headline *Di.xxv. Q.i*, although d. 24 runs on until halfway down the page.","certain")
n("n1143","s062-05","a relation that comes from within","en","translation","*respectus intrinsecus adueniens*; see the Latin note.")
